?     :print this help

<cr>  :open select node
o     :open select node
O     :open select node in vertical split window
t     :open select node in new tab
i     :open select node in split window
go    :Open selected file, but leave cursor in the ProjectTree
gc    :diff select node with current file
r     :refresh select node
x     :close parent node
s     :prompt to filter display node
z     :close edited file, if the current node is dir, close all file under it.
Z     :like above , but close the file even if it had been changed.
u     :move cursor to upper dir
m     :mark current node (for copy, delete , move etc.)
f     :search node content for prompted string.
F     :search node content for content in the vim search register.
>     :jump to next editing file
<     :jump to prev editing file
<C-j> :jump to next sibling
<C-k> :jump to prev sibling
e     :open select node with system default application(open directory in file explorer)
E     :open select node in terminal 
#     :toggle between current dir tree and bookmarks(use bm* command to manage bookmarks in Shext)

DD    :delete select dir or file
Dm    :delete marked dir or file
A     :prompt to add a dir or a file

ya    :yank select node absolute path to vim register
yr    :yank select node relative path to vim register
yn    :yank select node name to vim register

cc    :rename current file or dir
yy    :yank current file or dir
dd    :cut current file or dir
ym    :yank marked file or dir
dm    :cut marked file or dir
p     :paste yanked or cut file or dir under selected dir node
P     :paste file from system clipboar
YY    :yank current file or dir to system clipboar

C     :change root to select node
B     :change root back
U     :change root to upper dir
QQ    :dispse the project tree

DD,m,yy,dd maps also work in visual mode.

:PTreeWorkTree <name> :create a git worktree under ~/.too/worktrees/<project>/<name> and refresh the tree

:PTreeRootAdd [name] :save the current displayed root in ~/.vinja/ptree_roots.cfg
:PTreeRootRemove     :remove all saved aliases for the current displayed root
:ProjectTreeSelect   :locate/open a saved root (also <leader>ps)

These commands use this tab's displayed root (including C, U and B changes),
not the selected node or original project root. They work from any buffer,
even with the tree panel hidden; run :ProjectTree first if the tab has no tree.
Virtual workspace/workset/archive roots cannot be saved, but real directories
reached within them can. Add requires an existing directory; remove can clean
up an entry even if its directory has disappeared.

The default alias is the directory basename. Supply a name for same-basename
projects or directories whose names contain whitespace. Aliases must be nonempty,
contain no whitespace or '=', and not start with '#'. Conflicting aliases are
refused, never overwritten; an already-saved path is a no-op, not a new alias.
Equivalent paths (including symlinks) count as the same root.

Remove accepts no arguments and deletes configuration entries only, never files,
buffers, or the tree itself. Removing an unsaved root is a no-op. Comments and
unrelated configuration entries are preserved. Reopen :ProjectTreeSelect to see
changes immediately. Concurrent edits from multiple processes are not locked.
